pinyon-shift-fh1-render-test-v1
# Car physics oracle: the player's steering and partial brake at speed
# (docs/specs/CAR_PHYSICS.md, SPEC-CAR-PHYSICS). Free roam on acc9-stock
# (stock R34) as fh1-physics-launch-brake: full throttle from frame 1100
# (the car responds near 1180), then at about 20 m/s a quarter left stick
# for 25 frames and full left stick for 15, both with the throttle held,
# then the stick centred and the throttle off, and a partial brake
# (left trigger 115 of 255) for 40 frames. Run with
#   --game-argument=--pinyon_shift_physics_trace=6
#   --game-argument=--pinyon_shift_physics_oracle=true
#   --game-argument=--pinyon_shift_physics_oracle_snapshot_frame=1095
#   --game-argument=--pinyon_shift_physics_oracle_trace_ticks=800
# The body trace gives the steer control against the front wheels' angle
# (the speed-sensitive lock) and the brake value against the wheels'
# brake torque (the brake input curve) on the player's path.
# clock-hz 60
input 0 0000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 360 1000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 366 0000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 480 1000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 486 0000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 600 1000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 606 0000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 720 1000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 726 0000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 780 0000 0 0 0 0 0 0
wait 900 3000 vehicle
capture 1090 start
input 1100 0000 0 255 0 0 0 0
input 1400 0000 0 255 -8192 0 0 0
input 1425 0000 0 255 -32768 0 0 0
input 1440 0000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 1450 0000 115 0 0 0 0 0
input 1490 0000 0 0 0 0 0 0
capture 1560 end
stop 1570
